both get 4.\n\nI'm working through the payoffs under an updateless prior: pass on every input gives 2 years each, submit on every input gives 4, and mixing the two comes out lower on average. Since the copy is a child of the same policy, I'm settling on pass everywhere.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm treating this as a prisoner's dilemma, where two copies of the same policy get different inputs. The policy Φ has to cover every input, so my payoff depends on what it outputs for my input and for the other copy's input. If it says pass on everything, both get 2; if it says submit on both, both get 4.\n\nI'm working through the payoffs under an updateless prior: pass on every input gives 2 years each, submit on every input gives 4, and mixing the two comes out lower on average. Since the copy is a child of the same policy, I'm settling on pass everywhere.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9899,"completion_tokens":890,"total_tokens":10789,"cost":0.057396,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.057396,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.039596,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0178},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":417,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}